    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Palak Paneer Recipe [Instant Pot]",
      "description": "Indian food is delicious, and curries are the ultimate comfort food, but sometimes they aren’t the healthiest. This keto-friendly instant pot palak paneer is an exception. It’s easy to make, packed with flavors and spices, and contains all the benefits of spinach.\n\nThe star of the show is the paneer cheese. It’s super high in protein and full of calcium, iron, and fat, meaning you’ll feel fuller for longer. Because of this, paneer cheese is a popular protein substitute in curries for vegetarians. The vibrant green color comes from the spinach. This leafy green veggie is loaded with vitamins and full of fiber to help keep your digestion optimum. Fresh spinach is recommended; however, frozen spinach is a secondary option if you don’t have any fresh ones on hand.\n\nThe intense and delicious taste comes from the inclusion of many spices and herbs, like cumin seeds, garam masala, coriander powder, garlic, and paprika, which give that traditional Indian curry flavor. Add a generous helping of fresh ginger and a serrano pepper for a kick and mouth-watering spice. If you are not good with spicy food, you can reduce the amount based on your preferences.\n\nThis palak paneer pairs perfectly with the light and flavorful cumin cauliflower rice as a white rice substitute. Cauliflower has a subtle flavor, and it absorbs all the rich spices from the curry.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\nPalak Paneer:\n4 tablespoon butter\n1 teaspoon cumin seeds\n2 teaspoon garam masala\n1 teaspoon ground coriander\n1 teaspoon paprika\n1 teaspoon sea salt, or to taste\n1 medium serrano pepper\n1/2 medium onion, chopped\n4 teaspoon fresh garlic, minced\n3 1/2 ounce fresh tomatoes\n16 ounce spinach\n1/4 cup water\n16 ounce paneer packet\n\nCauliflower Rice:\n3 tablespoon butter\n1 teaspoon cumin seeds\n1 teaspoon garam masala\n480 gram cauliflower, riced\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 6 servings of Keto Instant Pot Palak Paneer. Each serving comes out to be 415 calories, 33.4g fat, 7.6g net carbs, and 20.8g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
